      "title": "Recruit",
      "description": "Stefan E. Warschawski Math Fellowship (JPF04618) - UC San Diego AP On-Line Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Stefan E. Warschawski Math Fellowship (JPF04618) Stefan E. Warschawski Math Fellowship Apply now to Stefan E. Warschawski Math Fellowship Job #JPF04618 MATHEMATICS / Physical Sciences / UC San Diego Position overview Position title: SEW Math Fellow Salary range: A reasonable salary estimate for this position is $88,300. ​ The posted UC academic salary scales (https://www.ucop.edu/academic-personnel-programs/compensation/2025-26-academic-salary-scales.html) set the minimum pay determined by level at appointment. See the following table for the salary scale for this position : Table 23 Application Window Open date: September 1, 2026 Next review date: Monday, Nov 2, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Mathematics ( Department of Mathematics, UC San Diego ), within the School of Physical Sciences at the University of California, San Diego, is committed to academic excellence and diversity within the faculty, staff and student body.  We invite applications for our Stefan E. Warschawski Math Fellowships in all areas of Mathematics, Statistics, and related topics.  All positions are subject to availability of funding.  These positions are aimed at new and recent PhDs whose work demonstrates strong potential in mathematical research. These positions are three-year nonrenewable appointments. Teaching in Mathematics, Statistics, and related topics will be expected, and the teaching load is four quarter courses per year.  Lecture courses will be at the undergraduate upper and lower division levels. Total duration of an individual’s postdoctoral service may not exceed five years, including postdoctoral service at other institutions. The International Union, United Automobile, Aerospace and Agricultural Implement Workers of America (UAW) is the exclusive representative of the postdoctoral scholars. [PX Contract][(https://postdoc.ucsd.edu/postdocs/px-contract.htm)] More Info : http://www.math.ucsd.edu Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Currently pursuing PhD in Mathematics, Statistics, or related field, with evidence of PhD  degree completion by July 1, 2027. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) PhD degree by July 1, 2027. Application Requirements Document requirements AMS Standard Cover Sheet -   available for free on mathjobs.org Statement of Research Statement of Teaching Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Publication list Cover Letter (Optional) Reference requirements 3 letters of reference required at least one letter should address teaching in depth Apply link: https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04618 Help contact: math-apstaff-g@ucsd.edu About UC San Diego The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a university employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California prohibits smoking and tobacco use at all of its university-controlled properties. The UC San Diego Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is available online at: https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf . This report provides crime 