    "https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04635": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full SpecialistApply nowto Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist (JPF04635) - UC San Diego AP On-Line Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist (JPF04635) Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist Apply now to Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist Job #JPF04635 MARINE PHYSICAL LABORATORY / Scripps Institution of Oceanography / UC San Diego Position overview Position title: Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist Salary range: Salary range: A reasonable salary range estimate for this position is $63,500 - $93,200. The posted UC academic salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See the following table for the salary scales for the position: Specialist Application Window Open date: September 4, 2026 Next review date: Saturday, Sep 19, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Saturday, Sep 4, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Marine Physical Laboratory (MPL) within the Scripps Institution of Oceanography at UC San Diego invites applications for a Specialist position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist in ocean acoustics and marine bioacoustics. The position will contribute to the development, coordination, and execution of collaborative research programs focused on underwater acoustics, passive acoustic monitoring, marine bioacoustics, and associated ocean observing technologies. The Assistant, Associate, or  Full Specialist will provide substantial independent input into the planning and execution of research projects and will play a central role in coordinating multidisciplinary research activities. Responsibilities will include development of research concepts and project objectives; preparation of research proposals, technical reports, and other scientific documentation; coordination of project teams and collaborative activities; and oversight of project timelines, deliverables, and financial resources. The position will also contribute directly to research and dissemination of research findings. This may include participation in acoustic data analysis and interpretation, synthesis of results across project components, development of scientific presentations, and substantial contributions to peer-reviewed publications, particularly through manuscript development, scientific writing, and editing. Key Responsibilities: • Provide scientific and organizational leadership for research projects in ocean acoustics and marine bioacoustics, including project planning, implementation, tracking of milestones, and coordination of deliverables. • Contribute to the development of new research concepts, collaborations, and funding opportunities. • Prepare and contribute to research proposals, project reports, technical documentation, and other scientific products. • Coordinate multidisciplinary research teams and communication among investigators, technical personnel, collaborators, sponsors, and partner organizations. • Assist with oversight of project budgets, expenditures, resource allocation, and planning in coordination with administrative staff and principal investigators. • Contribute to the analysis, interpretation, and synthesis of research data as appropriate to individual projects. • Contribute substantially to peer-reviewed publications, including development of manuscripts and scientific writing and editing. • Present and disseminate research findings through publications, reports, presentations, workshops, and other professional activities. • Participate in professional activities and University and/or public service relevant to ocean acoustics, marine bioacoustics, and the research programs supported by the position. The Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist is expected to demonstrate professional competence and activity and to contribute to the scientific and professional community in their area of expertise. Appointment level/rank will be based on the candidate’s background and experience. A link to the full description of the Specialist series is provided for your review: Specialist (APM-330) Department : https://scripps.ucsd.edu/mpl Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Master’s degree (or equivalent) or a Ph.D. in Oceanography required. • Candidates with a Master’s degree (or equivalent) are eligible to apply only for the Assistant or Associate Specialist ranks. • Candidates with a Ph.D. (or equivalent research doctorate) are eligible to apply for any rank; the Full Specialist rank requires a Ph.D. (or equivalent research doctorate). •    Candidates must have a record of academic or research accomplishments that includes contributions to published or in-press research. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) • Demonstrated experience in ocean acoustics, marine bioacoustics, passive acoustic monitoring, or a closely related area. • Experience contributing to the planning, coordination, and execution of scientific research projects. • Demonstrated experience in scientific or technical writing, including preparation of research reports, proposals, publications, or comparable scientific products. • Demonstrated record of professional activity and University and/or public service relevant to the candidate’s area of expertise. Preferred qualifications • Experience coordinating multidisciplinary or multi-institutional research projects. • Experience developing research proposals and contributing to externally funded research programs. • Experience with project budgeting, financial tracking, and coordination of research resources. • Experience with underwater acoustic data analysis, acoustic instrumentation, ocean observing systems, or associated analytical approaches. • Strong record of scientific publication and demonstrated experience in manuscript development, writing, and editing. • Excellent organizational and communication skills and demonstrated ability to coordinate effectively among investigators, research staff, collaborators, sponsors, and administrative personnel. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Research List of Publications -   Include a current list of publications (Optional) Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Please provide contact information (e.g. home institution, email, website, etc.) Apply link: https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04635 Help contact: t7nguyen@ucsd.edu About UC San Diego The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a university employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California prohibits smoking and tobacco use at all of its university-controlled properties. The UC San Diego Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is available online at: https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf . This report provides crime and fire statistics, as well as institutional policy statements & procedures. Contact the UC San Diego Police Department at (858) 534-4361 if you want to obtain paper copies of this report. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct, are currently being investigated for misconduct, left a position during an investigation for alleged misconduct, or have filed an appeal with a previous employer. Click for more information on Assembly Bill-810 Click for more information on Senate Bill-791 • “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. • UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy: [ https://policy.ucop.edu/doc/4000385/SVSH ] • UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties: [ https://policy.ucop.edu/doc/1001004/Anti-Discrimination ] Job location San Diego, CA Apply now to Assistant, Associate, or Full Specialist or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, San Diego is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, San Diego is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports AP On-Line Recruit University of California, San Diego Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04637": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Project Scientist Regenerative Neuroscience Research (JPF04637)",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Project Scientist Regenerative Neuroscience Research (JPF04637) - UC San Diego AP On-Line Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant, Associate, or Full Project Scientist Regenerative Neuroscience Research (JPF04637) Assistant, Associate, or Full Project Scientist Regenerative Neuroscience Research Apply now to Assistant, Associate, or Full Project Scientist Regenerative Neuroscience Research Job #JPF04637 OPHTHALMOLOGY / School of Medicine / UC San Diego Position overview Position title: Project Scientist Salary range: A reasonable salary range estimate for this position is $74,100 - $113,600. The posted UC Academic Salary Scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See the following table for the salary scale for the position: Project Scientist Application Window Open date: August 24, 2026 Next review date: Tuesday, Sep 8, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Tuesday, Aug 24, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The University of California San Diego, Department of Ophthalmology , is committed to academic excellence among faculty, staff, and students and seeks to recruit project scientists wishing to join an established team of scientists that is researching molecular mechanisms that confer resilience on cell types that selectively degenerate in inherited retinal disorders and control retinal ganglion cell regeneration and postnatal hypothalamic neurogenesis. The selected candidates will be responsible for performing studies and will provide onsite teaching and mentoring of students and staff. In addition, the selected candidates will draft manuscripts, prepare presentations, present at conferences and participate in grant writing. Appointments will be at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Project Scientist level based on background and years of experience. A link to full description of the Project Scientist series is provided for your review: Project Scientist (APM-311) Department : https://oph.ucsd.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidates must have a PhD or MD/PhD in Neuroscience, Developmental or Cell Biology or other health-related fields. Preferred qualifications Candidates with at least 5 years experience in generating, breeding, and genotyping transgenic are preferred. Candidate with at least 5 years of experience in brain and retinal histological techniques (immunohistochemistry and in situ hybridization) and/or working with iPSC-derived retinal organoid preparations are preferred. Candidates with at least 4 years of experience using Visium/Xenium-based spatial transcriptomics are preferred. Candidates with at least 2 years experience in generating and analyzing single-cell RNA-Seq data from both primary retinal tissue and retinal organoids are preferred. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Misc / Additional (Optional) Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://apol-recruit.ucsd.edu/JPF04637 Help contact: mpack@health.ucsd.edu About UC San Diego The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a university employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California prohibits smoking and tobacco use at all of its university-controlled properties. The UC San Diego Annual Security & Fire Safety Report is available online at: https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf . This report provides crime and fire statistics, as well as institutional policy statements & procedures. Contact the UC San Diego Police Department at (858) 534-4361 if you want to obtain paper copies of this report. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct, are currently being investigated for misconduct, left a position during an investigation for alleged misconduct, or have filed an appeal with a previous employer. Click for more information on Assembly Bill-810 Click for more information on Senate Bill-791 • “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. • UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy: [ https://policy.ucop.edu/doc/4000385/SVSH ] • UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties: [ https://policy.ucop.edu/doc/1001004/Anti-Discrimination ] Job location San Diego, CA Apply now to Assistant, Associate, or Full Project Scientist Regenerative Neuroscience Research or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, San Diego is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, San Diego is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports AP On-Line Recruit University of California, San Diego Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
